# * import, and print --new, with .latest files, as upstream does them
# (expectations from the reference hledger; fixtures in import/)

# ** 1. Each file's latest date is remembered with how many transactions it had, in .latest.FILE;
# a later import takes only the transactions after those (same-date counts).
$ D=$(mktemp -d) && cp import/a.j $D && cp import/bank.csv $D && cp import/bank.csv.rules $D && cd $D && hledger -f a.j import bank.csv 2>e; s=$?; sed "s|$D|D|" e; cat .latest.bank.csv; printf '2020-01-02,taxi,7\n2020-01-03,rent,500\n' >>bank.csv; hledger -f a.j import bank.csv 2>e; s=$?; sed "s|$D|D|" e; cat .latest.bank.csv; cat a.j; cd /; rm -rf $D; exit $s
imported 3 new transactions from bank.csv to D/a.j
